WEBVTT

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.360
Make sure you drive safely, okay?

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.780
What's wrong, Yakumo-kun?

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.870
Please take care of Yakumo.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:16.700
Of course.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:22.540
Oh, but I don't really help Yakumo much, I just follow him around.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.250
No, that's all you need to do.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.000
Please continue to support Yakumo.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.510
Isshin-san?

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:43.980
The doctor gave me a diagnosis.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.860
She said I will at most have six months left.

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:03.120
I'm surprised they granted us permission so soon.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.750
Yes, it was rather unexpected.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:11.630
However, I believe the hospital also sees that this issue should be resolved with the utmost urgency.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:16.050
Apparently the ghost asks our patients,

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.050
"When will you die?"

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.100
Even though they gave us permission to investigate, there are still a lot of restrictions.

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:28.190
So there are rooms that are off limits.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:31.110
Oh, we have to turn off our cell phones too.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:36.610
Go faster, idiot!

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.910
What exactly happened?

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:42.330
That bitch mentioned something totally outrageous.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.540
Nanase Miyuki?

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.920
She said that Yakumo's father will kill him... Isshin.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:52.710
What? But he's a...

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:55.130
You're trying to say a ghost, right?

00:01:55.130 --> 00:02:00.930
There were no logs of him speaking to Nanase Miyuki via her cell.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:04.720
I believe he cannot and does not need to use a cell phone.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.230
Because he's a ghost-

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.270
Leave that for later.

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:11.610
So? Have you informed Isshin-san?

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.070
What about Yakumo-shi?

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.030
Neither of them are answering which is why I'm in such a rush!

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.530
You're going the wrong direction. It's this way.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.380
Don't you think he's acting rather strange today?

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:34.550
Maybe it's...

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.130
Mother...

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.470
So that's what happened...

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.890
He's been like that ever since.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.980
Perhaps we should have chosen another day...

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.690
Detective Goto, he's back.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.490
Where were you?!

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.950
I was eating out with Nao.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.820
We need to eat out now and then too, you know.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:07.290
Why are you being so carefree in your current situation?

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.660
Ishii-kun's told me.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.960
I hear that <i>he</i> plans to kill me.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:15.210
Yeah...

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:16.880
Well,

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.090
shall we wait and see how things turn out?

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.840
I've asked Ishii to guard Nao.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:27.350
Although he's unreliable, he's better than nothing.

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:30.060
Have you informed Yakumo?

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.100
I can't seem to get a hold of him.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.190
You needn't worry about him anymore.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.690
Haruka-chan's there for him.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:40.490
What?

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:46.870
Goto-kun, if something happens to me, please take care of Nao.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.540
Don't curse yourself!

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:53.000
Besides, you hate me, don't you?

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.000
That's not true.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.340
No, I've known it all along.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:04.010
You hate the fact that I drag Yakumo into my investigations.

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.260
At first, yes.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.470
But not anymore.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.810
You're a man I can trust.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.770
Wh-What's that?

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:18.440
I also like the fact that you're boorish.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.900
Bastard, enough of the teasing-

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.700
Bastard!

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:31.040
I'm sorry, Goto-kun.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.290
Why...

00:04:57.610 --> 00:05:00.770
I believe this is the first time we've met in person.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:11.990
I'm his guardian, and you're his real father.

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.750
Can we talk a little

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:19.130
before you kill me?

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.300
That should have been closed.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:56.250
Even though I'm a monk, there was a darkness whirling inside of me - darker than the night.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:58.670
My hatred towards you.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.750
Enmity.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:09.890
You left my sister in hell,

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:14.310
and burdened Yakumo with a painful dark karma.

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:20.770
There were numerous times where I just wanted to kill you with my own bare hands.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:26.780
However, those emotions of mine have long since disappeared.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:32.160
It's ironic.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:37.540
Something I could not see, no matter how hard I tried, just appeared in front of me out of the blue.

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:42.500
Give up.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:49.800
No matter how hard you try, Yakumo will never fall into the hands of darkness.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:54.810
In exchange, I will also...

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.900
Yakumo-kun, l-look!

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.070
What's the meaning of this?

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:18.950
Are you all right?

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:22.540
Well, she just apologized to me for the other night.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:23.420
What?

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.670
This is bad!

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:32.720
Hey, Ishii!

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:33.680
Ishii!

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:43.980
Hey, Mister! Mister!

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:45.020
Can you hear me?!

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:47.020
Hey! If you can, say something!

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.820
Good, you're still alive.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:55.070
That's enough.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:56.740
I'll hear you out later.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:58.080
Don't say anything else.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.120
Don't just stand there! Call an ambulance!

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.540
Y-Yes, sir!

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.210
Don't cry! He won't die.

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.880
I won't let him, so don't cry!

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.800
Don't die, Mister.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:19.680
Stay here and help with the investigation when the police arrive.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:20.680
Understand?

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.020
Yes, sir.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:34.950
That ghost was completely different to all those ghosts I've seen up until now.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:40.080
The patient mentioned that he had met the same ghost before.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:43.250
He said that when he previously met her, she asked him when he'd die,

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:45.250
but this time, she apologized.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:49.290
Does this mean that the ghost has turned over a new leaf?

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:50.550
Makoto-san?

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.260
I'm sending a text to my company.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:53.720
Just wait a minute, okay?

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:57.640
Aren't we supposed to keep our cell phones switched off?

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.100
We're allowed to use them here.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:05.730
It's from Ishii-san.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:07.770
Yes, this is Ozawa.

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:10.360
What?

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:12.110
Isshin-san did?

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:20.700
I believe he tried to persuade him from his course...

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:24.200
For the sake of all those who will be left behind once he passes away.

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.000
What?

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:31.000
At most, he had a year left to live.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:32.590
No way...

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.510
That was his doctor's prognosis.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:39.890
Then the reason you've been acting so strange is...

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:42.260
In front of you!

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:54.990
Are you all right?

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:55.990
Y-Yes...

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:00.620
Oh, Goto-san.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:01.530
Yes.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.870
We're heading back to the temple right now.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.500
Hold on.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.330
Turn around immediately.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:11.750
They're taking Isshin-san to the hospital we were just at.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:14.050
Isn't that it?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.440
You can cry now.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:36.280
You've done well.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:42.030
Even though I was with him... I'm sorry.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.420
How's Isshin-san?

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:53.040
He's lost too much blood.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:55.710
There wasn't enough blood left to circulate in his body.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:59.300
I'm afraid his brain has ceased functioning.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:04.810
Even with a mechanical ventilator, his heart is barely beating.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:09.310
Unfortunately, there's no chance of him making a recovery.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:18.150
You mean...

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.070
Brain dead?

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:24.950
I'll arrest you!

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:30.910
If you don't want to be arrested, then reoperate immediately!

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:32.790
Goto-san, please calm down.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:33.960
Shut up!

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.960
Please stop, Goto-san.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:54.480
Isshin-san is... brain dead...

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:10.500
I wonder if Nao-chan understands...

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:15.330
He can't answer her no matter how many times she calls him.

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:24.010
I can't believe this. Nor do I want to believe it's true.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:28.220
I mean, see? He looks like he's going to wake up at any moment...

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.020
Yet...

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:34.440
Arai-sensei.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:36.150
Is his family here?

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:39.570
There's something I'd like to talk to you about.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:40.900
Please come this way.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.240
Hey, Yakumo.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:45.910
I'll take care of Nao.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:48.780
You're okay with that, right?

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:53.290
You're also okay with that, right?

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.800
I'm home.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.840
Welcome home.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:10.060
My, we have some cute guests.

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.100
Nice to meet you.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.100
Come in.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:15.310
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:16.600
Okay.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.520
Make sure you eat supper, okay?

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:28.620
Then it wasn't a coincidence that you were here?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:29.450
No.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.540
We've got witnesses.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:35.120
The neighbors have seen the man we believe to be the culprit.

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:38.130
Now we can be positive that he's the culprit.

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:47.680
Um, how's Nao-chan?

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:50.140
She must've been really mentally exhausted.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.350
She fell asleep the moment her head hit the pillow.

00:13:54.470 --> 00:14:00.310
It's been a while since I've had tea with someone this late.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:04.070
Goto-san doesn't come home a lot, does he?

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:05.070
Yes,

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:08.110
but it's the same whether he comes home or not.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:11.160
We don't really talk.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.330
If we had a kid, maybe things would've been different...

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:19.080
Nao-chan must be a strong girl.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:19.920
Yes, she is.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.750
Women need to be strong.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:25.590
Men just pretend to be strong.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:29.800
They shoulder all the burdens by themselves,

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:35.180
yet, in reality, they don't like being alone.

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.430
They need someone with them.

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:40.690
I think I can understand that.

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:57.620
I've been ordered by my boss not to write about Isshin-san's stabbing.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:59.540
It's not just newspapers.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.830
They've even banned it from being broadcast.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:04.790
What's the meaning of this?

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:09.010
The supervisor who was originally in charge of the Nanase Murders

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:11.840
is now an administrator at headquarters.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:19.430
If Nanase Miyuki causes any more trouble, it'll affect his reputation too.

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:20.980
So that's why they've put pressure on all the media...

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.730
Exactly.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:25.270
And it's not just what happened yesterday.

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:29.610
They haven't even publicized the fact that Nanase Miyuki foretold the attempted murder.

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:42.170
Let's start with the main temple at the back.

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:45.380
I hear that forensics already looked at that.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:47.630
What do you expect <i>me</i> to do?

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:52.470
Detective Goto?

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:56.680
He's as deaf as a bear's ear instead of a donkey, eh?

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:56.680
Note: There's a Japanese idiom that says, "Giving him advice is as useful as praying into a donkey's ear."

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.410
Yakumo-kun...

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:25.130
Last night, I stayed over at Goto-san's house with Nao-chan.

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:33.170
Although Goto-san pretty much left straight after, his wife Atsuko-san is there, so she'll be all right.

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:41.180
Sorry for asking you to do forensics' job.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.440
Did you find anything?

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:48.270
I did... but I can't really make sense of it.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.770
What do you mean?

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:55.740
Did you really see the man in the sunglasses in this area?

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:57.450
Yeah, I'm positive.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:01.450
There are no footprints whatsoever.

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:04.330
That's not all.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:11.340
I was also unable to discover any traces of this soil at the crime scene inside the main temple.

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:15.220
What do you think that means?

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:18.390
That there's a possibility that another culprit was involved.

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:20.220
That's not all.

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:27.480
According to Yakumo-kun, ghosts are like clusters of emotions.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:31.230
They cannot have any physical belongings.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.740
Perhaps that man is...

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.920
I'm so happy.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:50.840
So we're going to become one.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.340
What's wrong?!

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:15.110
Leaving that story aside...

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:19.410
We'll re-investigate his tracks and-

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.710
What's the meaning of this?

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:31.670
You may go home.

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.630
You're to go home at your scheduled finishing time for a while.

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:34.880
What?

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:36.380
You've got to be kidding me.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:37.630
Why do I have to do something like that?

00:18:37.630 --> 00:18:39.550
Ishii told me about it.

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:42.890
You're taking care of the victim's daughter, right?

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:45.890
S-So what?

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.600
Her name's Nao-chan, right?

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:51.100
Be with her for her sake.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:53.860
But, Miya-san, I can't do anything-

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:55.650
You don't have to do anything.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:59.740
All you've got to do is be with her.

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.670
My, you're home really early today.

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:11.670
How rare.

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:14.710
Apparently that's you.

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:15.670
This is?

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.420
It looks like a bear.

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:20.720
Roar!

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:26.180
Ro-ar!

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:32.940
I'm going for a smoke.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:50.080
Mister, you've got such a cute girl waiting for you.

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:52.870
Wake up already!

00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:12.480
Yakumo-kun, here...

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:33.830
My eye brings suffering to others,

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:36.630
and I too, am suffering.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:43.380
Then I shall also walk the path where others will view me with wary eyes.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:10.160
Thank you.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:16.170
You finally spoke.
